Now it is evening.
I walk to the nearby bus stand.
There is a bus to my place there.
I get on the bus.
I ask the conductor.
"Does this bus go to Kakkanad?"
He says, "Yes, come inside."
"Sit near that window."
I sit there.
The bus goes straight.
Then it turns right.
I look outside.
These roads are familiar to me.
After a little while the bus turns left.
Now I understand this city.
My place and the waterfront are close to each other.
The way from Marine Drive to my home is easy.
I like Kochi very much.
I go home happily.
